<title>SINGAPORE: Inchcape 1996 net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Inchcape 1996 net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in million Singapore dollars unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		48.52  vs    58.56</p>
<p>    Group shares (cent)	   29.60  vs    35.80</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		10.00  vs    10.00</p>
<p>    Special dividend (cents)    10.00  vs    10.00</p>
<p>    Turnover (bln)		   1.24  vs     1.32</p>
<p>    Interest income		  5.90  vs     6.32</p>
<p>    Interest expense		 9.41  vs     7.21</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		   75.72  vs    88.48</p>
<p>    Tax				 22.74  vs    25.93</p>
<p>    Minorities			(4.46) vs    (3.99)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  3.73  vs    (7.32)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay/register	June 27/June 12</p>
<p>Note: Trading and investment holding group Inchcape Bhd said its extraordinary item came from sale of a residential property offset against provisions made for an indemnity for the disposal of its office automation business, loan to a third party and cost of restructuring Inchcape Shipping Services.</p>
<p>--Singapore newroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
